      "text": "To find the first digit of the base $8$ representation for $473_{10}$, we start by dividing out the next power of 8 from 473:\n\n\\[\n473 \\div 8 = 59 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 3\n\\]\n\nConsequently,\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n    \\ \\ \\ 59 \\\\\n  \\underline{\\overline{473 \\div 8}} \\\\\n        35\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nNow, we repeat this process with 35, dividing by the smallest power of 8 (which is 8 itself):\n\n\\[\n35 \\div 8 = 4 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of} \\quad 3\n\\]\n\nSubstituting back into the operation:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n    \\ \\ \\ 4 \\times 8 = 32 \\\\\n    \\underline{35 - 32} \\\\\n        3\n    \\end{array}\n\\]\n\nHence, the base $8$ representation for 473 is $43_8$.\n\nLooking at the base $8$ representation $43_8$, it is evident that the first digit is $4$.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
